`/home/daniel/spring-petclinic-rest-long-degradation-test/work/202608011310/officefloor-just-solve-chain0/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/GeneralExceptionHandler.java`
```java
private static final Logger logger = LoggerFactory.getLogger(GeneralExceptionHandler.class);
...
logger.error("Unexpected error", ex);
```

**Test-side capture harness** for asserting AUDIT output:

`/home/daniel/spring-petclinic-rest-long-degradation-test/work/202608011310/officefloor-just-solve-chain0/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AuditLogCapture.java` — an `AutoCloseable` that attaches a Logback `ListAppender` to the `"AUDIT"` logger (default constructor uses name `"AUDIT"`). Key methods:
- `messages()` — formatted messages of all captured events.
- `anyContains(String... substrings)` — true if some event contains all substrings.
- `anyAtLevel(String level, String... substrings)` — true if some event **at the given level** (e.g. `"WARN"`) contains all substrings.
- `count()`.

No `WARN`-level AUDIT logging exists anywhere in `src/main` yet — the only AUDIT call is the `info` in `AuditOwnerCreation`. (Confirmed: a search for `areaCode`/`area code`/`WARN` in `src/main` returned only unrelated `@SuppressWarnings("unchecked")` hits.)

## 4. Owner entity and OwnerRepository

**Entity: `/home/daniel/spring-petclinic-rest-long-degradation-test/work/202608011310/officefloor-just-solve-chain0/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`** (extends `Person`, which provides `firstName`/`lastName`). Relevant field + getter for telephone:
```java
@Column(name = "telephone")
@NotEmpty
@Digits(fraction = 0, integer = 10)
@Pattern(regexp = "^[0-9]{10}$", message = "Phone number must be exactly 10 digits")
private String telephone;

public String getTelephone() { return this.telephone; }
```
Other getters available: `getAddress`, `getCity`, `getEmail`, `getRegistrationDate`, `getMembershipNumber`, `getCustomerCode`, `getMembershipTier`, `getNamesakeCount`, `getSharesHousehold`, `getLocality`, `getPets`, plus `getId()`/`isNew()` from the base entity. Telephone is constrained to exactly 10 digits, so the "area code" = first 3 digits is well-defined.

**Repository: `/home/daniel/spring-petclinic-rest-long-degradation-test/work/202608011310/officefloor-just-solve-chain0/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/OwnerRepository.java`** — interface methods:
```java
Collection<Owner> findByLastName(String lastName) throws DataAccessException;
Page<Owner> findByLastName(String lastName, Pageable pageable) throws DataAccessException;
Owner findById(int id) throws DataAccessException;
void save(Owner owner) throws DataAccessException;
Collection<Owner> findAll() throws DataAccessException;               // list ALL owners
Page<Owner> findAll(Pageable pageable) throws DataAccessException;
void delete(Owner owner) throws DataAccessException;
```
There is **no `findByTelephone` method**. Every chain function that needs to inspect other owners (city limit, daily limit, duplicate telephone, namesake, etc.) uses `findAll()` and filters in memory — that is the established pattern to follow for any telephone/area-code lookup. Implementations exist at:
- `.../repository/jpa/JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl.java`
- `.../repository/jdbc/JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl.java`
- `.../repository/springdatajpa/SpringDataOwnerRepository.java`

## 5. Existing tests for creating owners (telephone / audit / warn)

Acceptance tests use black-box `POST /api/owners`. Base class: `/home/daniel/spring-petclinic-rest-long-degradation-test/work/202608011310/officefloor-just-solve-chain0/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java`. Key helpers: `ownerNode()` (fully-valid unique owner), `createOwnerOk(body)` (posts, asserts 2xx, returns id), `seq()` (unique counter), `uniqueTelephone()` = `String.format("2%09d", seq())`. Authenticated as `acceptance-admin` via `@WithMockUser`; each test is `@Transactional` (rolled back).

**Audit test — `/home/daniel/spring-petclinic-rest-long-degradation-test/work/202608011310/officefloor-just-solve-chain0/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/Cp19Tests.java`** (cp19: every creation logs user + owner id to AUDIT):
```java
@Test
void coreAuditsOwnerCreation() throws Exception {
    try (AuditLogCapture audit = new AuditLogCapture()) {
        int id = createOwnerOk(ownerNode());
        assertTrue(audit.anyContains("acceptance-admin", String.valueOf(id)),
                "audit should record the user and the new owner id; got " + audit.messages());
    }
}
```

**Telephone-area-code WARN test — `/home/daniel/spring-petclinic-rest-long-degradation-test/work/202608011310/officefloor-just-solve-chain0/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/Cp20Tests.java`** (cp20: WARN to AUDIT when a new owner's area code — first 3 digits — is shared by 5+ existing owners). This is the test that exercises telephone area-code + WARN audit logging, and there is currently no production code implementing it:
```java
private void createWithAreaCode(String area) throws Exception {
    ObjectNode o = ownerNode();
    o.put("telephone", String.format(area + "%07d", seq())); // unique 10-digit, shared 3-digit area
    createOwnerOk(o);
}

@Test
void coreWarnsOnBulkAreaCode() throws Exception {
    try (AuditLogCapture audit = new AuditLogCapture()) {
        for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
            createWithAreaCode("571");
        }
        createWithAreaCode("571"); // 6th — now 5 existing share the area code
        assertTrue(audit.anyAtLevel("WARN"),
                "expected a WARN audit for a bulk signup; got " + audit.messages());
    }
}

@Test
void functionalityNoWarnBelowThreshold() throws Exception {
    try (AuditLogCapture audit = new AuditLogCapture()) {
        createWithAreaCode("572");
        createWithAreaCode("572");
        createWithAreaCode("572"); // only 2 existing share the area code
        assertFalse(audit.anyAtLevel("WARN"),
                "no WARN expected when fewer than 5 owners share the area code");
    }
}
```

There is also a unit-level controller test `/home/daniel/spring-petclinic-rest-long-degradation-test/work/202608011310/officefloor-just-solve-chain0/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1Tests.java` (Spring-arm controller tests), but the audit/telephone-warn behavior is covered by the acceptance `Cp19Tests`/`Cp20Tests` above.

### Summary of what this implies
The `Cp20Tests` expects a `WARN`-level message on the `"AUDIT"` logger when a newly-created owner's telephone area code (first 3 digits, telephone is exactly 10 digits and normalized to digits-only in `BuildOwner`) is already shared by **5 or more** existing owners (threshold: WARN fires on the 6th such owner). To implement it following existing patterns you would add a new function class in `.../rest/function/owner/`, wire it into `owners.POST.yml` (naturally after `SaveOwner`, near/at the `AuditOwnerCreation` step), use `LoggerFactory.getLogger("AUDIT")` and log at `.warn(...)`, and count matching owners via `ownerRepository.findAll()` comparing the first 3 telephone digits.

